32: /**
33:  * A helper for creating a base dir programmatically, typically at test time.
34:  * <p>
35:  * This is typically used in conjunction with {@link EmbeddedApp}, when the app requires a base dir.
36:  * It is however also useful for any kind of testing where a “filesystem” is needed just for the test.
37:  * <p>
38:  * The {@link #tmpDir()}, {@link #dir(File)}, {@link #tmpJar()} and {@link #jar(File)} methods create instances,
39:  * controlling what file system space will be used.
40:  * <p>
41:  * The {@link #write(String, String)}, {@link #mkdir(String)} and {@link #path(String)} methods can be used for creating and getting at content.
42:  * <p>
43:  * The {@link #getRoot()} method provides a path object for the root of the base dir.
44:  * <p>
45:  * This type implements {@link Closeable}.
46:  * Closing an embedded base dir causes the base dir to be <b>removed</b> from the real file system.
47:  * It is generally always desirable to close the base dir in order not to leave files around.
48:  * The {@link #use(Action)} method allows an action to be executed before having the base dir be automatically closed.
49:  */
